  "notes": "The boom-bap-adjacent corner of this lane, and it is authored as three departures from the ratchet spine: the swing goes to 0.58 (audible swing on a 2&4 snare), `velocityVar` drops to 0.08 (the research says low velocity variance explicitly), and the hats go to 8ths with occasional 16th doubles instead of the lane’s continuous 16ths. F♯ major leads the key weights, which the research calls unusually frequent for the lane, and the scale list carries mixolydian so the modal ambiguity on the psychedelic cuts is reachable. ⛔ The bass is `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.94 with `glideProb` 0.04 and no passing tones — the research says a sustained sub or filtered synth moving in whole and half notes, harmonic support rather than a hook, and this is the honest engine spelling of that: `reese_sustain` emits one note per chord and saturates. Over a kick that plays only 1 and the and-of-2, two low roots a bar reads as sustained at 90–95. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium and marks the drum and texture claims [LOW-CONF] — the whole `drums` block below except the tempo band is inferred from the lane, and the ghost-snare positions in particular are an invention of the reading. ⚠ The hat roll sits at freqPerBar 0.20, the floor of this batch’s band, because the research says no trap rolls at 90–95; it is reachable only because a model that declares a roll block owes every seed a reachable roll. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.6 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.6 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub.",
